From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Add the Epson S1C33 architecture, and trace NOMMU programs from their start

The C33 is a no-MMU FDPIC port with the generic 32-bit system call table
and 64-bit time only.  int 0 takes the number in r4 and arguments in
r6-r11 and returns the result in r4; the kernel keeps the number in
orig_r4, which tracers read and rewrite.  Its one architecture-specific
call is 244, c33_set_tls.  clone takes its arguments in the generic order.

Without an MMU the tracee is started by vfork, and a seizing tracer can
attach only once the exec is under way; on a single core the program has
often made its first calls by then, or finished.  On NOMMU, have the
child use PTRACE_TRACEME before the exec and skip the SIGTRAP that exec
then stops it with, so a trace starts at the program's first call.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index ff10fd5..7d36fbc 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6378,6 +6378,12 @@ bfin)
 
 printf "%s\n" "#define BFIN 1" >>confdefs.h
 
+	;;
+c33*)
+	arch=c33
+
+printf "%s\n" "#define C33 1" >>confdefs.h
+
 	;;
 csky*)
 	arch=csky
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 956bb85..89e1b0d 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@ bfin)
 	arch_enable_Werror=no
 	AC_DEFINE([BFIN], 1, [Define for the Blackfin architecture.])
 	;;
+c33*)
+	arch=c33
+	AC_DEFINE([C33], 1, [Define for the Epson S1C33 architecture.])
+	;;
 csky*)
 	arch=csky
 	AC_DEFINE([CSKY], 1, [Define for the C-SKY architecture])
